Header
  - name := Shared E
/* An object @E shared by several universes (`-cop'): an active object which holds it, inline
   (`Flat'). Each call of a slot of @E from another universe is a message, executed in its
   universe one after the other: mutual exclusion, without lock. A slot without result is
   asynchronous (`add_last'), a slot with a result is synchronous (`count': it waits for the
   previous messages). What goes in or out must be a value, an immutable object or an active
   object (else, an error at the compilation); a block (`foreach') cannot be sent.
   Each call is atomic, not a sequence of calls: for a composed operation, a slot of an heir.
   `Insert': a @Shared @E is not an @E, the messages cannot be bypassed.
     m := Shared (Array Int) .new
     m.add_last 1
     m.count.print
*/
Insert

  + parent_e:Flat E

Public

  - new:Self <- clone
